    {
      "id": "revision_concordant_industry_latency",
      "name": "Revision-Concordant Industry Latency",
      "class_name": "",
      "description": "Computes each stock's leave-one-out industry excess-return impulse and a causal lag-one loading on that impulse. It ranks under- or over-assimilation gaps only when the predicted industry response and a fresh dual-channel fundamental event have the same sign.",
      "formula": "",
      "trading_idea": "Industry basket flows transmit broad peer information unevenly, so a stock can lag the response implied by its historically estimated lagged loading on an industry impulse. This child trades that propagation gap only when a fresh earnings, revenue-estimate, or reported-surprise signal agrees with the direction of the implied industry response, treating the fundamental update as an authenticity filter rather than trading every peer-flow dislocation. The interaction carries edge because the industry model identifies which names have not yet assimilated a common shock, while the revision state distinguishes informative read-through from transient ETF, hedge, or unrelated common-risk pressure.",
