    {
      "id": "industry_hawkes_innovation_fragility_lag",
      "name": "Industry Innovation Fragility Lag",
      "class_name": "",
      "description": "Computes an idiosyncratic downside-event innovation relative to a lagged multichannel intensity forecast, aggregates that innovation across leave-one-out industry peers, and gates it by the target's lack of immediate downside participation and working-capital/financing fragility. Higher values indicate unpriced downside contagion risk.",
      "formula": "",
      "trading_idea": "An unexpected, volume- and range-confirmed downside event in economically close peers is more informative than ordinary peer selling because it represents a fresh contagion impulse rather than predictable clustered volatility. The child identifies firms that have not yet absorbed that peer Hawkes-style innovation and whose expanding receivables/inventory, leverage, and weak cash buffer make them especially exposed to the same funding or demand shock. Neither parent alone isolates this intersection: event innovation identifies when the peer shock is genuinely new, while balance-sheet susceptibility identifies which delayed receivers should transmit it into a six-day repricing.",
