    {
      "id": "sector_jump_echo_unabsorbed_receiver",
      "name": "Sector Jump Echo Receiver",
      "class_name": "",
      "description": "For each stock, compute a leave-one-out sector basket return and volume surprise over recent days, emphasize synchronized peer jump days, and subtract the stock's own contemporaneous normalized response. Rank the signed residual only when peer shock breadth is high and the stock's volume/range response indicates it can absorb the adjustment.",
      "formula": "",
      "trading_idea": "Information and liquidity shocks often arrive first in the most actively traded names of a sector, while related names adjust with a delay. The signal identifies stocks whose sector peers experienced a synchronized large return-and-volume impulse but whose own return has not yet reflected the peer move, conditional on the stock having normal trading capacity rather than a liquidity vacuum. The trade is falsified if delayed receivers do not subsequently converge toward the direction of the sector shock, or if apparent laggards instead systematically reflect firm-specific news. This extends graph-based relative-value intuition from the supplied graph-clustering paper, but uses a causal leave-one-out sector shock as the local graph state.",
