      "id": "issued_supply_sector_catchup_absorption",
      "name": "Issued Supply Sector Catch-up Absorption",
      "class_name": "",
      "description": "Computes a leave-one-out sector impulse and rolling beta-implied three-day response deficit, then conditions positive deficits on a recent positive net-stock-issuance state, decelerating signed-volume selling pressure, and intrabar recovery. The output cross-sectionally ranks eligible supply-masked sector laggards.",
      "formula": "",
      "trading_idea": "Positive sector impulses are initially incorporated through liquid leaders, while an issuer with a fresh disclosed equity-supply state can lag because mechanical distribution temporarily offsets sector-information buying. The child buys only those positive-sector-response deficits whose issuer-specific selling pressure is demonstrably decelerating and whose bar closes recover toward the high, identifying absorption rather than adverse-information selling. Parent A detects delayed sector assimilation but cannot distinguish ordinary underreaction from financing-related pressure; Parent B identifies temporary issuance pressure but lacks an external information anchor, so their interaction isolates the release point at which masked sector news should catch up.",
