    {
      "id": "concentrated_flow_price_inertia",
      "name": "Concentrated Flow Price Inertia",
      "class_name": "",
      "description": "Computes directional close-location-weighted participation, its temporal concentration and directional coherence, then favors pressure that remains unpriced relative to its trailing return path. High values indicate concentrated latent buy pressure absorbed with little permanent displacement; low values indicate the symmetric sell state.",
      "formula": "",
      "trading_idea": "A temporally concentrated sequence of same-direction close-location/volume pressure is a daily-bar proxy for a parent order being worked through the market. When that pressure has produced little net price displacement relative to the path's total variation, passive liquidity has temporarily absorbed the order rather than resolved the imbalance, so remaining execution and dealer inventory transfer should push returns in the pressure direction over the next six days. The edge can persist because daily bars do not reveal trade sign, hidden liquidity, or the remaining parent-order schedule, while inventory-averse intermediaries adjust exposure gradually. This is falsified if concentrated, directionally coherent, low-efficiency flow has no stronger same-direction 6-day return than equally directional flow that has already moved efficiently.",
